body:
@bryevdv I fully agree that providing more input from the user side is needed to keep an OSS project running. What I will do is to provide my codebase once its an a good shape. I am using bokeh to display timelines that reload upon panning, could be quite of interest to others.

And yes, I am working on an application making use of bokeh server; I tried though to set up a simple notebook script to demonstrate the error, but that won't work, as it needs the server interaction.

@mattpap I implemented your suggestions to change line 1050 of bokeh/core/properties.py to
value = dateutil.parser.parse(value.split(' (')[0]).date()

Now the error does not show up in the browser nor in the bokeh server log, but the on_change callback is still not reached (I had put a `import pdb; pdb.set_trace()` at the first line of the callback function to make sure).
